followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JoshuaMarcondes/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JoshuaMarcondes/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JoshuaMarcondes/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JoshuaMarcondes/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JoshuaMarcondes/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JoshuaMarcondes/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JoshuaMarcondes/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JoshuaMarcondes/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-09-18T16:14:29Z","updated_at":"2025-09-18T20:25:17Z","body":"> I have encountered this bug in 2D as well. Using Direct3d 12 doesn't allow there to be more than one light casting shadows. The first placed light is always the \"active\" one. Disabling it enables shadows on the next light over, but shadows can never render from more than one light source.\n\nYou're right, in 3D this bug not only breaks the omnilight shadows, but it also breaks the shadows of other spotlights.\n\n<img width=\"1523\" height=\"871\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/f4a05286-6f60-4a6e-9074-e3959681a8b1\" />","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3308362013/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]